# Text input, chance, and variables that follow the player between NPCs.
# Binds to every Klops merchant. Spawn one with:  /npc spawn Klops_Merchant

npc: Klops_Merchant
title: Madame Klops
speaker: Madame Klops
portrait: Pages/RespawnPageSkull@2x.png

start: known when $player.true_name
start: stranger

== stranger
The cards told me a stranger would come today. They did not tell me your name.
<<input $tmp.answer "What do they call you?">>
<<if $tmp.answer == "">>
  A silent one. The cards dislike silence.
  <<jump reading>>
<<endif>>
<<set $player.true_name = $tmp.answer>>
So. {$player.true_name}. Every merchant in these lands will know it by nightfall.
<<jump reading>>

== known
Ah, {$player.true_name}. The cards have been restless since you left.
<<jump reading>>

== reading
<<set $npc.readings = $npc.readings + 1>>
-> Read my fortune.
    <<jump fortune>>
-> Who else have you read for?
    <<if $npc.readings > 1>>
      You are the {$npc.readings}th to sit at this table. The others did not all leave smiling.
    <<else>>
      You are my first today. A fresh deck for a fresh face.
    <<endif>>
-> What do you sell?
    Charms, trinkets, and things best not asked about.
    <<shop>>
-> Enough of this.
    The cards will wait. They always do.
    <<end>>

== fortune
<<if chance(0.5)>>
  Fortune smiles. A gift, so the cards remember me kindly.
  <<give Food_Popcorn 2>>
<<else>>
  The cards are dark today. Keep your coin and your courage close.
<<endif>>
-> Read them again.
    <<jump fortune>>
-> That's enough.
    <<jump reading>>
